===persian===

های... تو را دوست دارم...
شهرِ شعرم را
در کنار رودِ تو ساختم
از من بگذر...
رود مرداب نیست
اگر بازایستی...
ویرانه خواهم شد...
زمستان ۱۳۶۸

===machine===

Hey... I love you...
I built the city of my poem
beside your river
Pass on past me...
A river is no marsh
if you come to a standstill...
I will be left a ruin...
Winter 1368

===lantern===

Hey... I love you...
I built the city of my poem
beside your river.
Pass me by...
A river is no marsh.
If you come to a standstill
I will be left a ruin...

Winter 1368

===translation===

===footnotes===

از من بگذر is two things at once: "pass on past me" and "forgive me." The poem
needs both readings — he is asking to be flowed past, because a river that stops being a river
is a marsh, and the city he built on its bank falls down. Asking the beloved to keep leaving is
the same sentence as asking to be forgiven.

